# Formatting for the C sources under c_src/ and test/c/.
#
#   make format           # rewrite Erlang (erlfmt) and C (clang-format) sources
#   make check-formatted  # verify both; part of `make check-fast`, which CI runs
#
# Deliberately close to stock LLVM style -- the clang-format default and the
# most widely recognised C/C++ convention -- so that the layout is whatever a C
# programmer would expect rather than anything specific to this project. Three
# overrides:
#
#   IndentWidth       LLVM uses 2, which is a C++ habit; 4 is the norm in C.
#   ColumnLimit       LLVM uses 80, which wraps awkwardly given how long the
#                     `enif_*` identifiers are at a 4-space indent.
#   PointerAlignment  `broker_t* broker`, not `broker_t *broker`. Both are
#                     common; this is the project's preference.
#   BreakBeforeBraces Stroustrup: `else` starts its own line rather than
#                     cuddling as `} else {`, and function opening braces go on
#                     their own line (the K&R/Linux convention for functions).
#                     Braces on if/for/while stay attached.
#
# Everything else is stock: casts with no following space (`(void**)out`),
# binary operators at the end of the wrapped line, and sorted include blocks.
#
# Blocks whose alignment carries meaning (the ATOM_LIST X-macro table) are
# fenced with `/* clang-format off */` ... `/* clang-format on */`. The marker
# comment must contain nothing but the directive.
---
Language: Cpp
BasedOnStyle: LLVM
IndentWidth: 4
ColumnLimit: 100
PointerAlignment: Left
DerivePointerAlignment: false
BreakBeforeBraces: Stroustrup
